From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.services.store: StoreContext of a machine with no Store account -- no products, unlicensed, nothing bought

There was no Windows.Services.Store: programs from the Microsoft Store that ask StoreContext about their licence or add-ons got "class not registered", and NanaZip (its sponsor check runs on a thread of its own once its toolbar is loaded) ended with an uncaught exception. New windows.services.store.dll: StoreContext answers as a Windows machine signed in to no Store account with nothing bought would -- GetDefault/GetForUser; GetStoreProductsAsync, GetAssociatedStoreProductsAsync(WithPaging), GetUserCollectionAsync(WithPaging) give no products with ExtendedError S_OK; GetAppLicenseAsync an unlicensed, non-trial licence (no add-on licences); GetStoreProductForCurrentAppAsync no product; RequestPurchaseAsync NotPurchased; GetAppAndOptionalStorePackageUpdatesAsync no updates; customer IDs empty; consumables, optional-package licences and package downloads fail cleanly (E_NOTIMPL). Every answer is a completed operation and every call is logged. Interface identity (IIDs, vtable order) per windows-rs (MIT); parameterized IIDs computed from the type signatures; the implementation is ours.
---
